    <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>

    <p class="updated">Last Updated: June 13, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Cookie Policy explains how Anikawa ("we", "our", or "us") uses
      cookies and similar technologies when you visit or use our website.
    </p>

    <p>
      By continuing to use Anikawa, you agree to the use of cookies as described
      in this policy, subject to the choices available to you through your
      browser settings.
    </p>

    <h2>What Are Cookies?</h2>

    <p>
      Cookies are small text files stored on your device by your web browser.
      They help websites function properly, remember user preferences, improve
      performance, and provide analytics and advertising services.
    </p>

    <h2>How We Use Cookies</h2>

    <p>We use cookies for the following purposes:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>To maintain secure user login sessions.</li>
      <li>To authenticate users accessing their accounts.</li>
      <li>
        To remember user-specific features such as watchlists and viewing
        history.
      </li>
      <li>To analyze website usage and improve our services.</li>
      <li>
        To support advertising services provided by trusted third parties.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Types of Cookies We Use</h2>

    <div class="table-wrapper">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Cookie Type</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>

        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Essential Cookies</td>
            <td
              >Required for core website functionality, account authentication,
              and security.</td
            >
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Analytics Cookies</td>
            <td
              >Help us understand how visitors interact with our website using
              tools such as Google Analytics.</td
            >
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Advertising Cookies</td>
            <td
              >May be used by advertising partners, including Google AdSense, to
              display and measure advertisements.</td
            >
          </tr>

          <tr>
            <td>Preference Cookies</td>
            <td
              >Remember certain settings and improve your browsing experience.</td
            >
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Authentication Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      If you create an account or log in to Anikawa, we use an authentication
      cookie to keep you signed in and provide access to account-related
      features.
    </p>

    <p>
      This cookie is designed with security measures such as HTTP-only access,
      secure transmission, and an expiration period to help protect user
      accounts.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-Party Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      We may allow trusted third-party service providers to place cookies on
      your device. These providers may include:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Google Analytics, for website traffic measurement and performance
        analysis.
      </li>
      <li>
        Google AdSense, for displaying advertisements and measuring their
        effectiveness.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      These third parties may collect information in accordance with their own
      privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Managing Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      Most web browsers allow you to control cookies through browser settings.
      You may choose to block or delete cookies at any time.
    </p>

    <p>
      Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect the functionality
      and user experience of Anikawa.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Advertising Cookies</h2>

    <p>
      Google may use cookies to serve ads based on users' prior visits to this
      website and other websites.
    </p>

    <p>
      Users can learn more about how Google uses information from sites and apps
      by visiting Google's policies and may manage ad personalization through
      Google's Ad Settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Cookie Policy</h2>

    <p>
      We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect changes in
      legal requirements, technology, or our practices. Any updates will be
      posted on this page together with the revised effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact Us</h2>

    <p>
